Base: 764ca0cf88bce99a4403594f05f0b90f695830b3
Baseline note: this branch includes the integrated R0 fixes. These RED failures were
observed on that R1 starting point, not on the original 2026-09-24 audit baseline.
Production files were not changed for this evidence.

Registered exact test names (commands exited 0):

  rtk proxy go test ./internal/core -list '^(TestCancelClosesToolCallHistory|TestAgentHistoryIncludesSteeringAndFollowUp|TestAgentHistoryPairsParallelToolResultsByID|TestSubagentSendReportsDroppedMessage)$'
  TestCancelClosesToolCallHistory
  TestAgentHistoryIncludesSteeringAndFollowUp
  TestAgentHistoryPairsParallelToolResultsByID
  TestSubagentSendReportsDroppedMessage

  rtk proxy go test ./internal/cli -list '^TestAssemblyInterceptorsAreIsolated$'
  TestAssemblyInterceptorsAreIsolated

  rtk proxy go test ./internal/core -list '^TestLoopAgentInterceptorIsScopedToInstance$'
  TestLoopAgentInterceptorIsScopedToInstance

Targeted RED commands (both compiled and ran the named tests; exit 1):

  rtk env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 -count=1 ./internal/core -run '^(TestCancelClosesToolCallHistory|TestAgentHistoryIncludesSteeringAndFollowUp|TestAgentHistoryPairsParallelToolResultsByID|TestSubagentSendReportsDroppedMessage)$'
  exit=1
  TestCancelClosesToolCallHistory: Agent history contained the assistant tool call but zero tool receipts after cooperative cancellation.
  TestAgentHistoryIncludesSteeringAndFollowUp: the Loop consumed start, steering, and follow-up in order (confirmed from the mock call log), while Agent history retained only start.
  TestAgentHistoryPairsParallelToolResultsByID: Agent history retained no assistant tool-call group or paired tool receipts for the completed parallel calls.
  TestSubagentSendReportsDroppedMessage: after the inbox filled to capacity, Send("overflow") returned nil.

  rtk env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 -count=1 ./internal/cli -run '^TestAssemblyInterceptorsAreIsolated$'
  exit=1
  TestAssemblyInterceptorsAreIsolated: assembly A's active Plan Mode globally canceled assembly B's custom mutation; its executor call count was 0.

  rtk env GOMAXPROCS=2 go test -p 2 -count=1 ./internal/core -run '^TestLoopAgentInterceptorIsScopedToInstance$'
  exit=1
  TestLoopAgentInterceptorIsScopedToInstance: setting an interceptor on loop A caused loop B's same-named tool call to be canceled.

The assembly-isolation failure came from `assembleMiddleware` registering each
Assembly's Plan Mode and shell-hook interceptors in the process-global registry.
The new core test isolates the underlying API contract: `SetToolInterceptor`
must affect only the LoopAgent on which it was called. These tests were run
before changing production code.

